# KOVA — AI Pipeline & System Prompt

## Generation Architecture

The entire pipeline runs in the browser via Vercel AI SDK:

  User prompt -> buildSystemPrompt() assembles instructions
  -> ToolLoopAgent sends prompt + 92 tools to Anthropic
  -> via DirectChatTransport -> /api/ai-proxy (injects ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
  -> Claude responds with tool calls (primarily `render` JSX)
  -> Tools execute against FigmaAPI (scene graph) in browser
  -> Canvas re-renders in real-time
  -> ToolLoopAgent sends results back -> loop until done

There is NO custom backend generation route. NO compiler. NO intermediate format.

## use-chat.ts — The AI Core

Contains: SYSTEM_PROMPT constant, provider config, ToolLoopAgent, DirectChatTransport.

### buildSystemPrompt() pattern:
```typescript
function buildSystemPrompt(campaignType?: string, brandKit?: BrandKit): string {
  let prompt = SYSTEM_PROMPT  // OpenPencil's prompt — every word unchanged
  prompt += '\n\n' + EMAIL_DESIGN_GUIDELINES
  if (campaignType) prompt += '\n\n' + loadCampaignGuide(campaignType)
  if (brandKit) prompt += '\n\n' + formatBrandKit(brandKit)
  prompt += '\n\n' + EMAIL_JSX_PATTERNS
  prompt += '\n\n' + IMAGE_HANDLING_INSTRUCTIONS
  return prompt
}
```

The SYSTEM_PROMPT constant MUST remain word-for-word unchanged — every line of JSX
reference, layout rules, forbidden patterns, verification workflow stays intact.
buildSystemPrompt() only appends. Never replaces.

## The render Tool

- Primary creation method. One call creates a complete section with children/styles/layout.
- Use `render` for generation. Use granular tools (setFill, updateNode) for editing.
- Size limit: ~40 elements per call. Split across multiple render calls using parent_id.
- Call `describe` on every rendered node immediately after render. Fix issues before
  proceeding to the next section.
- `describe` returns semantic/structural data — it does NOT visually render. It cannot
  detect invisible text. After dark-background sections, explicitly verify all child
  text nodes have a light color. Never assume inheritance.
- For final verification, use `exportImage` to get a visual render.

## /api/ai-proxy

- Validates Supabase auth session.
- Checks generations_used < generations_limit.
- Injects ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from server environment.
- Forwards to Anthropic, streams response back.
- Increments generations_used on success.
- CRITICAL: @ai-sdk/anthropic appends /v1/messages to baseURL. The proxy must
  handle POST /api/ai-proxy/v1/messages — not just /api/ai-proxy.

## DirectChatTransport Limitation

No mid-stream reconnection. If a generation stream drops, it cannot resume.
Build a "Generation failed — retry?" UI that re-triggers from scratch.
Do NOT build resume or partial-recovery logic.

## Provider Settings Removal

When hiding/removing ProviderSettings, ProviderSelect, ProviderSetup:
  1. grep for every import and template usage across the entire codebase.
  2. Remove all imports and template usages first.
  3. Only then delete or stub the component files.
Reversing this order causes build errors.

## src/ai/tools.ts

Uses VALIBOT for all schema definitions, not Zod. If you must modify this file
or packages/core/src/tools/ai-adapter.ts, use valibot exclusively.
